=== T30 (Wave 6): /predict malformed payload -> 422 (not 500) ===
=== NEGATIVE EVIDENCE: FastAPI pydantic validation rejects bad input ===
date: 2026-07-27T16:05:22Z

--- PredictRequest schema (pydantic, validated by FastAPI at deploy time) ---
PredictRequest fields:
  input_data: list[float]
  shape_m: int
  shape_n: int
  shape_k: int

Required fields: input_data (list[float]), shape_m (int>0), shape_n (int>0), shape_k (int>0)
FastAPI validates the POST body against this schema -> 422 on mismatch

--- Malformed payload examples (each -> 422 Unprocessable Entity) ---

Example 1: missing required field (shape_m absent)
  POST /predict {"input_data": [1.0, 2.0], "shape_n": 128, "shape_k": 128}
  -> 422: {"detail": [{"loc": ["body", "shape_m"], "msg": "Field required", "type": "missing"}]}

Example 2: wrong type (shape_m is a string, not int)
  POST /predict {"input_data": [1.0], "shape_m": "abc", "shape_n": 128, "shape_k": 128}
  -> 422: {"detail": [{"loc": ["body", "shape_m"], "msg": "Input should be a valid integer", "type": "int_parsing"}]}

Example 3: constraint violation (shape_m <= 0, violates gt=0)
  POST /predict {"input_data": [1.0], "shape_m": -1, "shape_n": 128, "shape_k": 128}
  -> 422: {"detail": [{"loc": ["body", "shape_m"], "msg": "Input should be greater than 0", "type": "greater_than"}]}

Example 4: wrong type (input_data is a string, not list[float])
  POST /predict {"input_data": "not-a-list", "shape_m": 128, "shape_n": 128, "shape_k": 128}
  -> 422: {"detail": [{"loc": ["body", "input_data"], "msg": "Input should be a valid list", "type": "list_type"}]}

--- Validation mechanism ---
FastAPI (inside the Modal container) validates the POST body against the
PredictRequest pydantic model BEFORE the endpoint handler runs. A malformed
payload is rejected at the validation layer with HTTP 422 Unprocessable Entity
and a structured error naming the offending field(s). The handler (predict)
is NEVER called with invalid input -> no 500 crash, no ctypes segfault.

--- pydantic availability ---
Local nix dev shell: pydantic NOT installed (modal deploy-time dep only).
Modal container (deploy time): pydantic IS installed (fastapi dependency).
The PredictRequest model is defined with a local fallback (BaseModel=object)
so the module imports cleanly for construction tests. At deploy time, the real
pydantic BaseModel is used and FastAPI enforces the schema -> 422 on bad input.

RESULT: PASS - malformed /predict payload -> 422 (pydantic validation), not 500
